tekx 0.2
title "Everything at Once"
author "Ada Lovelace", affiliation: "University of London", email: "ada@example.org"
author "Charles Babbage", affiliation: "Cambridge"
date today
msc "11N36 (primary)"
keywords "integration, consistency"
numbering by section
running "Everything"
bibliography "refs.bib"

define operator Var
define norm2(v) as ||v||_2 read as "the two-norm of {v}"
define postulate like axiom titled "Postulate"
define lab as "the Analytical Engine Laboratory"

abstract
  We test that every part of tekx agrees with every other [@hooley; @landau, p. 3].

contents

section Introduction #intro

Work at {lab} showed^[A footnote with $x^2$ and a citation [@vallee].] that

    integral of e^(-x^2) dx from -infinity to infinity = sqrt pi   #gauss

and, by Theorem @main and (@gauss), the variance $Var X$ and $norm2(v)$ behave.

theorem "Main" #main
  For every $n >= 1$, $sum k for k from 1 to n = n(n + 1)/2$.

proof
  Induction on $n$.

lemma #lem
  The long identity

      (a + b)^4 = (a + b)^2 (a + b)^2 = (a^2 + 2 a b + b^2)(a^2 + 2 a b + b^2) = a^4 + 4 a^3 b + 6 a^2 b^2 + 4 a b^3 + b^4   #binom4

  holds.

theorem* "Unnumbered"
  An unnumbered statement, cited by Lemmas @lem and @main2.

postulate #post
  Every integral converges.

